// x-rerun-8-09 (variant of x-parallel-02, the unbounded ref expansion): a
// non-regular recursive typedef, whose self-reference applies the formal
// to a bigger type, hangs the checker. Each step of the coinductive walk
// meets a new pair T<['a, string, ..]> vs T<[i64, f64, string, ..]>, so the
// RefPair memo never closes. Env::deftype accepts the typedef (it is
// contractive: graphix-types/src/env.rs:1687 checks guardedness only).
// command: timeout -s KILL 20 graphix --check x-rerun-8-09.gx   (the LSP shares the path)
// expected: refused at the typedef (a recursive reference must apply the
//   formals unchanged), or the let checked at once
// observed: no answer, CPU-bound, killed by the timeout (exit 137); also
//   `let g = |t: T<'b>| -> T<['b, i64]> t` alone hangs
type T<'a> = {n: [T<['a, string]>, null], v: 'a};
let x: T<i64> = {n: null, v: 1};
let y: T<[i64, f64]> = x;
y.v
